{
  "_comment": [
    "CoreVideo Tiles `tiles` wire fixtures (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-22-mac-tiles.md Task 7).",
    "Windows is the oracle: native-shell/CoreVideoPro.WinUI.Tests/TilesFixtureTests.cs runs every case through",
    "ScenePersistenceService.FromPersisted -> TilesLayerPayloadBuilder.Build -> TilesLayerWire.From ->",
    "MediaCoreCommandBuilder.BuildSceneGraphCommand. The Mac twin is ShellTestsTiles testEveryTilesFixtureMatchesTheSwiftBuilder.",
    "Participant ids are BARE Zoom ids (TilesLayerPayloadBuilderTests explains why). If Windows disagrees, fix `expected`, never Windows.",
    "`settings` is a persisted Tiles object (camelCase, same keys on both platforms); slots carry the Mac `kind` and the Windows ShowInputKind name.",
    "Cases 6-10 cover manual holes/duplicates/exclusions, routed mode with local ids and omitted names, the eligible-mode rules (omitted ignored, pinned slots, a bare session id never seated), an ambiguous name and a degenerate wall rect."
